<p>This approach works great most of the time, but there are some edge case=
s with how the geohash boundary is handled that we should discuss with the =
interviewer.</p>
<p><strong>Boundary issues</strong></p>
<p>Geohashing guarantees that the longer a shared prefix is between two geo=
hashes, the closer they are. As shown in Figure 9, all the grids have a sha=
red prefix: 9q8zn.</p>
