<figcaption class=3D"py-1">Figure 20 Deploy LBS closer to the user</figcapt=
ion></div></figure>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"follow-up-question-filter-results-by-time-or-business-type">Follo=
w-up question: filter results by time or business type</h3>
<p>The interviewer might ask a follow-up question: how to return businesses=
 that are open now, or only return businesses that are restaurants?</p>
<p><strong>Candidate</strong>: When the world is divided into small grids w=
ith geohash or quadtree, the number of businesses returned from the search =
result is relatively small. Therefore, it is acceptable to return business =
IDs first, hydrate business objects, and filter them based on opening time =
or business type. This solution assumes opening time and business type are =
stored in the business table.</p>
<h3 id=3D"final-design-diagram">Final design diagram</h3>
<p>Putting everything together, we come up with the following design diagra=
m.</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: center=
;"><img alt=3D"Image represents a system architecture diagram for a busines=
